# Jobs in Russian: кем вы рабо́таете?
subtitle: "Say what you and others do in Russian, and where: кем вы рабо́таете? — я рабо́таю инжене́ром, медсестро́й в больни́це, продавцо́м в магази́не."
tags: ["russian","jobs","professions","кем вы работаете","russian vocabulary"]
teaches: ["vocabulary/jobs","grammar/with-ending"]
thumb: "band \"What do you do?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Studying in Russian: я изуча́ю ру́сский","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/78-russian-study.cast"}

